  "body": "Was stacked on #4365. #4365 merged on 2026-11-27; this branch then took `git merge origin/main` (clean) and a new gate. The diff against `main` is now the commit of this PR only.\n\n## What changed\n\nU11 of the tool library refit (#3663): the Recipes tab of the tool library window.\n\n- One line under the tabs says what a recipe is and which row operations take: \"One recipe for each work material. The ★ marks the stock material of this document (Aluminium 6061): operations take that row.\" Other texts tell when no row names the stock material, or when no material is stated.\n- A ★ stands in a narrow lead column on the row of the stock material in force. This is the stock material of the active setup, else the document material (`stock_material::in_force`). Operations use the same order. U5 marked the document material only.\n- Under the table, each row has one dimmed line with its derived values: \"= 226 m/min surface speed, 0.050 mm per tooth (Aluminium 6061)\". The lines are read-only. They are computed only when their input changes (frame-cost rule, #2238). The cache is `ToolLibraryView::recipes`. The U5 columns \"Vc\" and \"fz\" are removed: they stood right of Stepover and scrolled out of view.\n- The buttons stand on one row: **Add material…** (a menu of the materials without a row), **Suggest feeds and speeds** (a menu: the stock material first with the ★, then each material with a row) and **Copy recipes from tool…** (a menu of the other document tools). A disabled button or entry tells why on hover. A units note follows. Tool material and Flutes follow the note (U10 keeps them on this tab).\n- Each button writes the window's draft only. The editor's one Apply lands the draft as one `ChangeTool`, so each button is one undo step. No command is new, so no MCP tool is owed.\n- With the Recipes tab, the shared table does not draw its own \"Add material row\" button. Properties' Cutting data group keeps it.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/4337-recipes-tab.md`.\n\nFiles: `recipes_tab.rs`, the new `recipes_actions.rs` and `recipes_derived.rs`, `recipes_fill.rs`, the `Extra` hook in `tool_cutting_rows.rs`, one field in `state_tool_library_dialog.rs` and one `pub use` line in `state.rs`. Centre cutting stays where U10 puts it: this PR does not change `tool_settings_grid::cutting_base`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (#4365 head `b1365b233`, the U8 frame) and after, 1366 x 768, a three-flute carbide end mill with three material rows, document material Aluminium 6061:\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4385/before.png)\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4385/after.png)\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_recipes.rs` unless named):\n\n- `the_star_follows_the_stock_material` (new): the ★ stands on the Brass row of the document material, then on the Mild steel row when the setup stock states Mild steel. The first line names the material.\n- `the_derived_line_follows_rpm_and_feed` (new): a row's line changes with its rpm and with its feed; the other row's line stays; a still frame computes nothing; one change is one computation.\n- `add_material_is_one_undo_step` (new): Add material… writes the draft and queues nothing; Apply is one undo step; one undo restores the tool.\n- `suggest_fills_the_draft_and_apply_is_one_undo_step`, `copy_from_tool_copies_the_rows` (updated to the menus): each lands as one undo step.\n- `the_document_material_row_is_marked` (updated to the ★ and the derived line).\n- `layout_window_tool_editor` in `page_layout_tool_library.rs` (updated): the explanation heads the table; Material, Spindle rpm, Stepdown read left to right; Add, Suggest, Copy follow the table on one row; the units note follows them above Apply.\n- `recipes_derived::tests::the_derived_line_follows_rpm_and_feed` and `recipes_fill::tests::add_material_adds_one_row_for_a_new_material` (new unit tests).\n- `tool_library_mockup.rs`: the column check uses Stepover (the Vc and fz columns are gone).\n\n`#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 1961 before, 1966 after.\n\n## Gate\n\nFinal head `7ea9ab7b1` (the commit plus the merge of `origin/main`), lane mac-1 (Mac, `lanes run --needs app --pool`), log `gate-4385-7ea9ab7b1.log`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green. Steps: `ui build (--no-run)` ok; `ui suites: lib` ok (the pinning tests above are in it); `ui suites:` boundary, boundary_picks, catalog_render, contour_dxf_sketch, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files, waterjet_tool: each ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n- Before the merge, head `684831edf` had the same results with `--base b1365b233` (the #4365 head).\n- No post, toolpath or geometry changed, so the example catalog suites do not apply. The light lane was not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A pointer click on the widgets inside the table: in the test harness, a pointer click in this horizontally scrolling table does not reach its widgets (the existing Remove buttons alike). The menus and buttons under the table take pointer clicks in the tests.\n- An inch document: the inch text of the derived line is pinned by the unit test only.\n\nChangelog: The tool library's Recipes tab explains what a recipe is, marks the stock material's row with a star, shows the surface speed and chip load of each row, and has Add material, Suggest feeds and speeds, and Copy recipes from tool buttons.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4337\n",
